  "output_text": "**Functional Phenotype Assignments for Tumor-Infiltrating B-Cell Clusters**  \nBased on the top differentially expressed genes and ORA-enriched pathways (MSigDB_Hallmark_2020, KEGG_2021_Human) in each cluster, we propose the following functional phenotypes:\n\n1. **Cluster 1: Transitional/Naïve Follicular B Cells**  \n   – Key markers: high TCL1A, FCMR (Fc µR), FCER2 (CD23), CD72, and MHC II genes (HLA-DRB1/DRB5, HLA-DPB1)  \n   – Enriched pathways (ORA): “Myc Targets V1” (NES↑, 9/200 genes), antigen processing and presentation (HLA-DR/DP/A), Th1/Th2 differentiation  \n   – Interpretation: TCL1A and FCER2 define immature/transitional B cells poised for follicular entry; robust MHC II and Myc‐driven biosynthetic programs support antigen uptake and presentation in naïve/follicular compartments.\n\n2. **Cluster 2: Quiescent/Resting Naïve B Cells**  \n   – Key markers: LY86 (MD-1), BLK (B-lymphoid tyrosine kinase), LTB (lymphotoxin-β)  \n   – Enriched pathways (ORA): Allograft rejection, IL-6/JAK/STAT3 signaling, NF-κB signaling (driven largely by LTB)  \n   – Interpretation: Modest upregulation (log₂FC ≈ 0.3) of BLK and LY86 with LTB suggests a resting, homeostatic naïve B subset that has not yet engaged full activation or antigen presentation programs.\n\n3. **Cluster 3: Interferon-Activated/Inﬂammatory B Cells**  \n   – Key markers: DUSP4, CD82, CD86, ISG15, IFI44L, IFITM1, GBP4 and MHC II (HLA-DPA1/DPB1)  \n   – Enriched signatures (top DE genes): strong type I IFN response (multiple ISGs) and costimulatory molecules  \n   – Interpretation: A robust interferon-stimulated gene program and upregulation of CD86 point to an antiviral/inflammatory activation state—likely extrafollicular B cells responding to cytokine cues within the tumor microenvironment.\n\n4. **Cluster 4: Early Activated/Germinal-Center-Homing B Cells**  \n   – Key markers: CD69, CCR7, CXCR5, CD83, IRF8, BTG1, JUNB, FOXP1  \n   – Enriched functions (DE genes): NF-κB pathway effectors (REL, NFKBID), chemokine receptors for T-cell zone and follicle entry, immediate-early activation markers  \n   – Interpretation: High CD69 and chemokine receptors CCR7/CXCR5 indicate recent BCR engagement and directed migration toward T-cell/B-cell border or germinal center; CD83 and IRF8 further hallmark pre-GC activation.\n\n**Summary of Reasoning**  \n– Clusters 1 and 2 both express canonical naïve B-cell markers (TCL1A, BLK), but Cluster 1 co-upregulates antigen-presentation machinery and Myc targets, marking a transitional/follicular phenotype primed for activation.  \n– Cluster 2’s very modest fold-changes and absence of costimulatory or IFN genes define a quiescent/resting naïve pool.  \n– Cluster 3 uniquely harbors a strong type I interferon signature (ISG15, IFI44L, IFITM1) and CD86, consistent with an inflammatory/antiviral activation state.  \n– Cluster 4 combines early activation markers (CD69, CD83, JUNB) with follicle-homing receptors (CCR7, CXCR5) and NF-κB effectors, indicative of B cells newly activated and migrating into germinal centers.",
